    {
      "id": 11,
      "type": "text",
      "title": "How to read this dashboard",
      "description": "What is counted and what is not collected.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 33
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "\n**Built-in commands:** successful completions over the rolling 7 days, from Prometheus. Collection began with the Oracle worker metrics rollout, so the window is partial until 7 days have elapsed. A zero during this period means no successes recorded since collection started, not no earlier use. Every registered command appears at zero; Prometheus handles counter resets. Aliases count under the canonical command. Data older than Prometheus retention is unavailable.\n\n**Custom commands:** lifetime successful uses from PostgreSQL. This count survives bot restarts. Enabled commands with zero uses are surfaced above; disabled commands remain in the inventory.\n\n**Chat actions and bot replies:** durable PostgreSQL counts. Oracle bot reply sent/failed accounting began with the 2026-10-10 rollout; earlier Oracle replies were not counted and cannot be reconstructed. Until a new reply is sent or fails, the replies chart can be empty even when the bot is healthy. Twitch event intake counts EventSub/queued records, not each ordinary chat line.\n\n**Not measured:** ordinary chat text, unrecognized !commands, and failed/cooldown command attempts are not retained as command usage. A blank signal means no data was collected for it; it does not prove the feature is unused.\n",
        "code": {
          "language": "plaintext",
          "showLineNumbers": false,
          "showMiniMap": false
        }
      }
    }
  ]
}
